@startuml

salt
{
  <b>SEE THE CONVENTIONS A PARTY USES</b>  { Tenant: acme_corporation | Party: ACCOUS | Kinds: 26 }
  --
  {
    {
      <b>The party and what it holds</b>
      --
      Party owns: <b>2,155</b> rows across <b>22</b> party kinds
      Tenant shares: <b>216</b> rows across <b>4</b> tenant kinds
      [ Party: ACCOUS v ] | [ Search a kind: "^swap            " ]
      --
      {#
        Kind | Term cols | Rows | Owner | Where it came from
        average_ois | 4 | 5 | party | DQ publish
        cds | 22 | 4 | party | DQ publish
        commodity_future | 50 | 790 | party | DQ publish
        <b>swap</b> | 7 | <b>320</b> | party | DQ publish
        currency_pair | 8 | 179 | <b>tenant</b> | DQ publish (base bundle)
        ibor_index | 5 | 10 | <b>tenant</b> | DQ publish
        overnight_index | 4 | 23 | <b>tenant</b> | DQ publish
        tenor | 4 | 4 | <b>tenant</b> | copied at provisioning
        ... 18 more kinds ...
      }
      <i>No convention table has a name column. Names on this screen are derived from the terms.</i>
    } | {
      <b>swap</b>: 320 documents, 201 distinct term sets
      --
      {#
        Document | Terms in words | Version
        AED-SWAP | AED - ModifiedFollowing - 30/360 - settlement 2d | v1
        <b>AED-EIBOR-3M-SWAP</b> | the same terms as AED-SWAP | v1
        EUR-6M-SWAP | TARGET - ModifiedFollowing - ACT/360 - 6M | v3
        ... 317 more documents ...
      }
      201 names stand for 320 documents: 119 rows carry a name another row also carries.
      --
      <b>Which of these does a run take?</b>
      <b>Not recorded.</b> No table has a default marker.
      The one %default% column in refdata is pays_at_default_time on cds_convention,
      which is a credit-event business term and not a mark on a document.
      [ Change this kind... ]
    }
  }
  --
  {
    {
      <b>What the run's report binds</b>
      --
      {#
        Definition | Conventions configuration
        Headline Position | US conventions
        Large Exposures | US conventions
        ... 76 more definitions ...
      }
      --
      {#
        Configuration | Type | Definitions | Rows it carries
        <b>US conventions</b> | conventions | 22 | <b>0</b>
        UK conventions | conventions | 24 | 0
        HK conventions | conventions | 22 | 0
        Group conventions | conventions | 10 | 0
      }
      <i>A conventions configuration is a header with no children.</i>
      <i>No market binding, no parameter and no analytic hangs off it.</i>
    } | {
      <b>What the export actually writes</b>
      --
      The run's conventionsFile is written from <b>the party's whole</b>
      conventions document. The bound configuration's id is <b>not read</b>.
      --
      {#
        Read for the file | Value
        Party resolved | ACCOUS
        Configuration resolved | (none - not read)
        Party kinds written | 22, 2,155 rows
        Tenant kinds written | 4, 216 rows
      }
      <i>Four configuration names, one set of rows.</i>
      <i>Rebinding a report to a different configuration would change nothing.</i>
      --
      <b>Versions of EUR-6M-SWAP</b>  version: { v1 | v2 | <b>v3</b> }
      {#
        Field | v2 to v3
        Fixed Day Count Fraction | 30/360 -> ACT/360
        Sub-Periods Coupon Type | (empty) -> Compounding
      }
      <i>The history says when a term changed. No run records the version it read.</i>
    }
  }
}

@enduml
